course: dictionary
lesson: 8207
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Retire is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «Grandma retired from nursing after forty years» tells you she stopped working because of her age.
explain: In sport, retire means to stop playing. «The striker had to retire hurt in the second half» tells you he left the game because he was injured. The sentence is about a game, so the meaning is different.
explain: Ask: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence. «The police dog will retire and live with the family» still makes sense if you say it stops working and goes to live as a pet.
fact: «Retire» means to stop working, usually because you are older.
fact: In sport, «retire» means to stop playing, often because of an injury.
fact: «Retire for the night» is a formal way of saying go to bed.
fact: A «pension» is money saved during working life, to live on after retiring.
fact: A «retirement party» is a celebration for someone whose working life has ended.
exercise: «Pat the lollipop lady will retire at the end of the year.» What does retire mean here? | To play a game | To wake up early | To move house | *To stop working
exercise: «The striker had to retire hurt in the second half.» What does retire mean in sport? | To score a goal | *To stop playing because of an injury | To run faster | To go home for tea
exercise: «When they retire, police dogs often live with their handler.» Find and copy one word that tells you the dogs stop their job. | dogs | police | handler | *retire
test: «A pension is money saved during working life, to live on after retiring.» What might a pension help someone do? | Work harder | Win a race | *Live on after they stop working | Play sport
test: Which sentence uses retire to mean go to bed? | Dad said, «I will retire from the team» | «Dad said, I will retire for the night» | Dad said, «I will retire early for the job» | *Dad said, «I will retire for the night»
exam: «Most professional footballers retire in their 30s.» Why might an author choose retire instead of stop? | *It is a precise word for ending a sporting or working career | It is a short, plain word | It means to eat dinner | It is a longer word
